// STATUS: error
// CHECK: before
// connect takes two arguments. A call with a third argument is a runtime error
// that halts the program, as for every built-in with a fixed arity
// (spec/05-stdlib.md, connect_within). The limit belongs to connect_within.
var l = listen("127.0.0.1", 0);
print "before";
connect("127.0.0.1", l.port(), 1);
print "after";
